# Build inputs. These generate the HTML that ships; they are not part of the
# site itself and must never be publicly served.
#
# data/ holds tax-rates.json, the source the rate tables and calculators are
# generated FROM. What ships to the browser is js/tax-rates.js, which build.py
# writes from it — serving the JSON too would put two copies of the same
# figures on the site, which is the exact problem this file solved.
build.py
site.json
content/
data/
